  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\n\nThe optimal step function h minimizes the maximum overlap integral C\u2085 by distributing its active regions to minimize alignment with its shifted complement. Starting from the initial_h_values (n=47), we employ a constrained optimization approach with the following strategy:\n\n- Use a gradient-based method with line search to update h while maintaining constraints.\n- Formulate the problem as minimizing the maximum cross-correlation.\n- clip and rescale h after each update to preserve feasibility.\n- Increase resolution gradually to capture finer patterns.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\n\nVariables:\n- h \u2208 \u211d\u207f, n = 47 initially, h[i] \u2208 [0,1]\n- \u222bh dx = 1 \u2192 sum(h) * dx =1\n\nObjective:\nMinimize C\u2085 = max\u2096 [corr(h, 1\u2212h, k)] * dx\nWhere corr is the cross-correlation at lag k.\n\nConstraints:\n0 \u2264 h[i] \u22641\nsum(h)*dx =1\n\nImplementation uses the cross-correlation computed as:\ncorr = np.correlate(h, 1\u2212h, mode=\"full\")\n\n3. Implementation procedure\n\na. Initialization\n- Take initial_h_values if available, else create a uniform distribution.\n- Set dx = 2.0 / n_points.\n- Initialize best_h = initial_h_values, best_C5 = evaluate.\n\nb. Gradient descent loop\n- Compute current C5 and its components.\n- Compute the gradient of the objective with respect to h.\n- Perform line search for step size.\n- Update h:\n   h = clip_and_rescale(h - \u03b1 * gradient)\n- Track best_h.\n\nc. Resolution increase\n- After certain steps, double n_points and interpolate h.\n- Refine solution at higher resolution.\n\nd. Termination\n- Stop when time budget exhausted.\n- Return best_h found.\n\n4. Search choices\n\n- Start with n=47, dx=2/47\u22480.0425\n- Increase to n=94, dx=0.021\n- Max iterations: 1000 with 600s budget\n- Learning rate \u03b1=0.01, decrease by 0.1 every 100 steps\n- Clip and project h after each update\n\n5. Compute budget\n\n- Initial evaluation: O(n)\n- Each gradient step: O(n\u00b2)\n- Line search: negligible\n- Expected 1000 iterations: O(1000n\u00b2)\n\n6. Validation\n\n- Ensure sum(h)*dx=1 \u00b11e-6\n- Check 0 \u2264 h \u22641\n- Recompute C\u2085 with evaluator to confirm.",
